{
  "id": "forming-te-form",
  "title": "Forming the て-form",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "content": "The **て-form** is one of the most versatile verb forms in Japanese. It acts as a connector between clauses and is the base for dozens of grammar patterns. Mastering it early pays off through all of N5 and beyond."
    },
    {
      "type": "transform_cards",
      "groups": [
        {
          "label": "Group 1",
          "tag": "く : ぐ",
          "rule": "く → いて / ぐ → いで",
          "rows": [
            {
              "base": "書く",
              "old": "く",
              "new": "いて",
              "result": "書いて",
              "romaji": "kaite",
              "english": "to write"
            },
            {
              "base": "泳ぐ",
              "old": "ぐ",
              "new": "いで",
              "result": "泳いで",
              "romaji": "oyoide",
              "english": "to swim"
            }
          ],
          "note": "Exception: 行く → 行って (not 行いて)"
        },
        {
          "label": "Group 1",
          "tag": "す",
          "rule": "す → して",
          "rows": [
            {
              "base": "話す",
              "old": "す",
              "new": "して",
              "result": "話して",
              "romaji": "hanashite",
              "english": "to speak"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "Group 1",
          "tag": "つ : る : う",
          "rule": "→ って (double consonant)",
          "rows": [
            {
              "base": "待つ",
              "old": "つ",
              "new": "って",
              "result": "待って",
              "romaji": "matte",
              "english": "to wait"
            },
            {
              "base": "帰る",
              "old": "る",
              "new": "って",
              "result": "帰って",
              "romaji": "kaette",
              "english": "to return"
            },
            {
              "base": "買う",
              "old": "う",
              "new": "って",
              "result": "買って",
              "romaji": "katte",
              "english": "to buy"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "Group 1",
          "tag": "む : ぬ : ぶ",
          "rule": "→ んで",
          "rows": [
            {
              "base": "飲む",
              "old": "む",
              "new": "んで",
              "result": "飲んで",
              "romaji": "nonde",
              "english": "to drink"
            },
            {
              "base": "遊ぶ",
              "old": "ぶ",
              "new": "んで",
              "result": "遊んで",
              "romaji": "asonde",
              "english": "to play"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "Group 2",
          "tag": "Ichidan",
          "rule": "remove る, add て",
          "rows": [
            {
              "base": "食べる",
              "old": "る",
              "new": "て",
              "result": "食べて",
              "romaji": "tabete",
              "english": "to eat"
            },
            {
              "base": "見る",
              "old": "る",
              "new": "て",
              "result": "見て",
              "romaji": "mite",
              "english": "to see"
            },
            {
              "base": "起きる",
              "old": "る",
              "new": "て",
              "result": "起きて",
              "romaji": "okite",
              "english": "to wake up"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "Group 3",
          "tag": "Irregular",
          "rows": [
            {
              "base": "する",
              "result": "して",
              "romaji": "shite",
              "english": "to do"
            },
            {
              "base": "来る",
              "result": "来て",
              "romaji": "kite",
              "english": "to come"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "content": "行く (to go) is the one Group 1 exception : it becomes 行って, not 行いて. Everything else follows the cards above without exception."
    }
  ]
}